WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.113
(bright music)

00:00:01.113 --> 00:00:02.490
- The Boeing VC-25

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:05.220
is perhaps the most
iconic plane in the world,

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.050
and it is of course the aircraft

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:10.080
that the US president most
often uses while traveling,

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.703
giving it the call sign Air Force One.

00:00:12.703 --> 00:00:14.730
(bright music continues)

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:17.310
But there is also a lesser known aircraft

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:20.250
that is just as vital
to the president, one

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.910
that hopefully would
never need to be used.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:28.440
This is the Boeing E-4B, better
known as the Doomsday Plane,

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:32.370
and its nickname is not
exaggerated, as the plane was made

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:33.971
for nuclear war.

00:00:33.971 --> 00:00:34.804
(energetic music)

00:00:34.804 --> 00:00:37.200
A plane built for the end of the world,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.130
designed to survive when
everything else fails,

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:44.340
able to command an
entire war from the sky,

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.960
and packed with technology
the public almost never sees.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.630
And for this video, I
digitally reconstructed

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:53.190
and mapped out the inside
(video whooshes)

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.140
of the aircraft to understand

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:58.263
how the Doomsday Plane actually works.

00:00:59.388 --> 00:01:01.110
(bright music)

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:05.490
The Doomsday Plane exists to
solve one very unique problem.

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:09.390
What if the United States
hit by a nuclear attack?

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:14.382
This hypothetical scenario
became very real during the 1950s

00:01:14.382 --> 00:01:18.120
and '60s when the Cold War
tension was at its peak.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.160
Both the US and the Soviet Union

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:23.490
were amassing massive
stockpiles of nuclear warheads,

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:26.250
and both nations were
proving that they can strike

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.530
the other nation, with the United States

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:31.170
stationing nuclear missiles in Europe,

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.480
and during the Cuban missile crisis,

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:37.410
the Soviet Union placing
their missiles in Cuba.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.720
During this time, the
United States established

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.940
a complex system of protocols

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:43.770
for how it would actually carry out

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.380
a nuclear strike against an enemy,

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:48.870
because in order to
authorize a nuclear strike,

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:53.070
there is one person, and one
person only who can do it,

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:56.130
and that is, of course, the president.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:57.810
The president's call with orders

00:01:57.810 --> 00:01:59.370
to strike would then be processed

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:01.200
for the US Strategic Air Command,

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:05.230
which is located at Offutt
Air Force Base in Nebraska.

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:06.063
(bright music continues)

00:02:06.063 --> 00:02:08.610
This location was chosen because
it is roughly in the middle

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:11.250
of the country and sits
well beyond the range

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:14.463
of hostile missiles or
nuclear armed bombers.

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:17.940
From this command center,
orders are carried out

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:20.730
to complete the strike
using any capability

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:22.950
of the US Nuclear Triad,

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:26.430
because the US has three main
ways in which it can launch

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:31.430
a nuclear strike, from land
using intercontinental missiles,

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:34.770
from the sea using nuclear submarines,

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:37.815
or from the air using bombers.

00:02:37.815 --> 00:02:39.180
(bright music)

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.400
So this is the chain of command used

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.580
to launch nuclear strikes in the US.

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.430
But there is one big
problem with this logic,

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.800
because all of this only works effectively

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.950
if the US launches the initial strike.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:57.720
But what if another nation
strikes the US first instead?

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:00.210
A nuclear detonation releases a wave

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:03.990
of electromagnetic pulses, or EMPs,

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:06.990
and such a blast can take
out the electrical grid

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:10.143
as well as any vulnerable
communication methods.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.830
This means that the
call from the president

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:17.130
might not reach its designated target.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.680
Additionally, important command centers

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.410
such as the Pentagon, the White House,

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:26.160
or even Offutt Air Force
Base itself might be targets

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.910
during a nuclear attack
and could be taken out.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.800
Therefore, the US wanted to prove

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:33.810
that even if they are hit first,

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:36.810
even if American cities, military bases

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:39.210
and command structure is wiped out,

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.760
they can still strike back.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:45.780
This idea became known as
mutually assured destruction.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.870
If any country does
attack the United States,

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:51.960
the US will be able to retaliate.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:56.040
And so Operation Looking
Glass was established.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:58.650
This is the name for a series of aircraft,

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:01.710
specifically EC-135s, that are designed

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:03.780
to take over nuclear command authority

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:07.050
should anything happen to
ground control at Offutt.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:09.030
Its name comes from its mission.

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:10.440
It is meant to mirror

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:14.370
or be a Looking Glass for ground control.

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:18.570
And so Boeing KC-135
Stratotankers were stripped

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:21.240
and retrofitted with
communications equipment

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:24.150
to make sure they have the
same capabilities in the air

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:26.160
as they would on the ground.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:30.000
But planes that are parked on
the ground are easy targets.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.020
And so beginning in 1961,
Operation Looking Glass goes

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:37.135
on 24/7 airborne alert.

00:04:37.135 --> 00:04:38.520
(energetic music)

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:39.930
This means that at least one

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:43.950
of these aircraft is in the
air at any given moment.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.860
This way, even if the
entire Looking Glass fleet

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:51.540
is destroyed, there will still
always be at least one EC-135

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:54.732
in the air that can take
over nuclear command.

00:04:54.732 --> 00:04:56.190
(bright music)

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:58.170
What is almost unbelievable to me

00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:00.390
is that this airborne alert lasted

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:04.987
for a staggering 29
years, from 1961 to 1990.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:11.220
For any given moment, day
or night, of those 29 years

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:15.630
of US history, there always
was at least one EC-135

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:19.920
in the air ready to
launch a nuclear strike.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:23.940
Only in 1990, just as the
Cold War was cooling down,

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:27.090
the constant airborne alert was halted.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:30.240
But even then, there's still
always at least one plane

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:33.453
that remains ready to
take off within minutes.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:39.440
Eventually in the 1970s, these
EC-135 aircraft were replaced

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:43.620
by a more modern Boeing
747-200s, retrofitted with all

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:45.480
of the communications equipment needed

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:49.200
to keep the president connected
to anywhere in the world.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:52.920
And these Boeing 747s make
up the Doomsday Plane fleet

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:56.130
that is still being used to this day.

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:58.320
So let's take a look inside to see

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:01.616
what makes this such a unique aircraft.

00:06:01.616 --> 00:06:03.600
(bright music)

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.340
Towards the very front of the plane,

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:07.998
there is a command office suite,

00:06:07.998 --> 00:06:11.100
basically a private area
reserved for any VIP

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.350
that may be traveling on the plane.

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:16.320
This is likely where the
president will take up quarters

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:18.390
should doomsday ever come,

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:21.450
but in practice, it is
actually most commonly used

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:23.220
by the Secretary of Defense,

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:24.870
because while traveling abroad,

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:28.110
the Secretary of Defense
typically flies using one

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:29.373
of these aircraft.

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:32.850
Just behind this suite is the galley,

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:35.190
or the flight attendant station.

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:38.010
And next to the galley is
a small conference room

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:40.050
where meetings can be held in flight,

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:43.170
almost like a flying situation room.

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:47.040
It seats up to nine people and
could very well be the room

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:49.950
where the fate of an
entire nation may be held

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:53.163
if the United States
ever enters nuclear war.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:57.540
Just beyond the conference
room is a briefing area.

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:00.990
Here, a podium is set up
so that leadership members

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:02.793
can address their staff.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:07.350
There are also multiple
phones, as maintaining contact

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:09.990
with military units, government agencies

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:12.510
and command centers
around the world is one

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:15.090
of the aircraft's primary missions.

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:18.390
And during foreign visits,
this area also doubles

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:21.390
as a press room where
journalists can be seated

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:24.363
and press conferences
can be held mid-flight.

00:07:25.752 --> 00:07:27.420
(bright music)

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:31.950
Continuing on past this room
is the Battle Staff Area.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:35.010
This is the largest room inside the plane.

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:37.470
Here, several workstations are set up,

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:39.450
and you'll find equipment you'd expect

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:42.990
to se in a typical office
setting, like computers, phones,

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:44.823
printers and copiers.

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:49.050
It is essentially a cubicle space.

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:52.860
From here, the military staff
can track unfolding events

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:56.883
and can help coordinate a
response to a national emergency.

00:07:58.350 --> 00:08:00.180
Just past the Battle Staff Area

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:03.030
is the communication section.

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:06.150
This is where the aircraft
communication specialists work

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:09.930
to maintain contact with
different military units.

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:11.430
The aircraft is equipped

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:14.520
with multiple redundant
communication systems,

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:16.860
and if one network becomes unavailable,

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:19.710
operators can quickly identify the issue

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:22.143
and switch to another system.

00:08:23.074 --> 00:08:24.720
(bright music)

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:26.160
Also monitored from here

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:29.340
is the aircraft's survivable
super high frequency,

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:31.470
or SHF system.

00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:34.950
This system is located in
the distinctive hump on top

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:38.280
of the aircraft, and inside
it, there is an antenna

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:40.830
that transmits very short radio waves

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:42.600
capable of carrying large amounts

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:45.990
of information across long distances.

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:49.740
This system is primarily used
to establish direct links

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:52.350
with US military satellites in orbit,

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:54.390
providing a highly secure means

00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:58.908
of communication even when
other networks are unavailable.

00:08:58.908 --> 00:09:00.150
(bright music)

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:03.300
And just below the
communications workstation

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:05.820
sits probably the most complex piece

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:09.390
of communications
equipment on this aircraft.

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:12.780
In the middle of this room
sits a compartment containing

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:15.540
a spool of antenna cable.

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:19.650
This cable can be deployed
while the aircraft is in flight.

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:23.220
Then the wire is reeled out
through the back of the plane

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:26.760
and it is trailing behind
it through the sky.

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:29.520
At full length, this antenna extends

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:32.241
a staggering five miles.

00:09:32.241 --> 00:09:33.510
(bright music)

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:35.430
This enormous length is needed

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:39.030
to create a very low frequency antenna.

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:43.170
Very low frequency radio
wavelengths are absolutely massive,

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:46.890
stretching for miles, and to
transmit them effectively,

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:48.060
you need an antenna

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:50.280
that is at least some meaningful fraction

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:52.140
of that wavelength.

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:53.880
When this antenna is in use,

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:57.600
the aircraft typically flies
in gentle banking turns,

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:59.610
which helps to keep the wire stable

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:03.300
and hanging in a more controlled
position behind the plane.

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:06.930
Basically, the jet has to
carefully fly in circles

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:10.273
while dragging the cable
behind and below it.

00:10:10.273 --> 00:10:11.640
(bright music)

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:14.400
The benefit of transmitting
at these frequencies

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:17.940
is that they can travel
incredibly long distances,

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:22.380
and more importantly, they can
partially penetrate seawater,

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:24.870
which means this aircraft
can communicate with one

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:28.710
of the most critical parts
of America's nuclear arsenal,

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:30.842
ballistic missile submarines,

00:10:30.842 --> 00:10:31.675
(video whooshes)

00:10:31.675 --> 00:10:33.144
hiding below the ocean.

00:10:33.144 --> 00:10:35.070
(bright music)

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:38.460
Two operators can sit
at the station to deploy

00:10:38.460 --> 00:10:42.480
and monitor the antenna, and
a periscope lets them see

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:45.930
the cable while it is trailing behind.

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:48.870
These operators can then
communicate with the pilots

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:50.940
to ensure that they
are flying the aircraft

00:10:50.940 --> 00:10:52.311
at the right speed and height

00:10:52.311 --> 00:10:56.705
to make sure turbulence
doesn't damage the antenna.

00:10:56.705 --> 00:10:57.960
(bright music)

00:10:57.960 --> 00:11:01.890
Located just above this
room is a small section

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:06.690
with additional seating as
well as the crew rest area.

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:10.140
The Doomsday Plane is capable
of mid-flight refueling

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:12.120
and is designed to stay in the air

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:14.820
for extended periods of time.

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:17.370
If necessary, the plane
can stay in the air

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:21.510
for an entire week without
ever needing to ground.

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:24.840
By that point, the aircraft
could have theoretically circled

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:29.840
the earth more than four times
all without a single stop.

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:33.150
The only reason the plane
would need to land after a week

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:36.075
is because the engines
would run out of lubricant.

00:11:36.075 --> 00:11:38.820
(bright music)

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:42.060
And just in case this rest
area isn't enough space,

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:44.760
there is an additional
one upstairs as well

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:47.190
just behind the cockpit.

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:48.960
One thing that sets this plane apart

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:51.540
from other Boeing 747s is that many

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:54.630
of the airplane systems
have been specially hardened

00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:57.780
to ensure that they can survive
the electromagnetic blast

00:11:57.780 --> 00:12:00.660
released during a nuclear strike.

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:03.780
The plane's windows are
covered in wire mesh

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:06.750
that helps prevent powerful
electromagnetic pulses

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:09.300
from damaging sensitive systems.

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:12.510
And even in a time of
modern glass cockpits, most

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:15.300
of the controls in this
plane remain analog,

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:18.240
another precaution to
protect the Doomsday Plane

00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:20.370
from a potential EMP blast

00:12:20.370 --> 00:12:23.763
that could disrupt sensitive
electronic equipment.

00:12:23.763 --> 00:12:26.370
(bright music)

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:28.620
Everything about the
Doomsday Plane is set up

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:31.290
to support the President
and Secretary of Defense

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:34.410
if the day of nuclear war ever comes.

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:36.720
It is an essential aspect of deterrence

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:40.590
for the United States, and
these are just the E-4B,

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:42.900
of which there are four aircraft.

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:45.603
These are operated by the US Air Force.

00:12:46.539 --> 00:12:47.372
(bright music)

00:12:47.372 --> 00:12:51.510
In addition, there are also
16 E-6 Mercury Aircraft

00:12:51.510 --> 00:12:53.850
that are operated by the US Navy

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:57.570
with somewhat overlapping
responsibilities.

00:12:57.570 --> 00:13:01.470
Together, these aircraft create
a highly redundant command

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:03.090
and control network.

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:05.910
If critical infrastructure
on the ground is damaged

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:09.360
or destroyed, many of the
same functions can be shifted

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:12.060
into the air, helping ensure that orders

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:13.500
can still be transmitted

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:16.899
and received during a national emergency.

00:13:16.899 --> 00:13:19.380
(bright music)

00:13:19.380 --> 00:13:22.290
To me, the airborne lake
of the Triad remains one

00:13:22.290 --> 00:13:26.190
of the most fascinating
elements of military technology,

00:13:26.190 --> 00:13:30.390
and no aircraft embodies this
better than the B-2 Spirit,

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:33.780
a bomber so advanced that
more than three decades

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:37.050
after its first flight, it
still looks like something

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:38.250
from the future.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:41.160
Capable, of flying at
high subsonic speeds,

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:43.350
the bomber can be anywhere in the world

00:13:43.350 --> 00:13:45.113
in less than half a day.

00:13:45.113 --> 00:13:47.280
(bright music)

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:48.870
My friends over at Mustard have made

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:50.850
an incredible documentary covering

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:52.800
